    "knowledge_point": "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
    "worked_solution": "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
